on-arrival: {!
Q.ziobro_whereabouts_stage = 5;
Q.ziobro_whereabouts_due_time =
    (Number(Q.time) || 0) + 3 + this.random.uint32() % 4;
Q.ziobro_whereabouts_updates += 1;
Q.ziobro_whereabouts_last =
    "Buenos Aires — unconfirmed, but already illustrated on every channel";
Q.news_headline =
    "A thoroughly unconfirmed Ziobro sighting reaches Buenos Aires";
!}

= [+ date_label +] — Buenos Aires, according to a photograph of a photograph

An airport photograph cropped until the airport is no longer visible, a voice
message forwarded beyond all knowledge of its sender and one Polish expatriate
who is *absolutely certain* now place Ziobro in **Buenos Aires**. No authority
confirms any part of this.

The photograph becomes less convincing every time somebody enlarges it. This
has no effect on the television schedule. Within the hour, every producer in
Warsaw has discovered stock footage of the Obelisk and booked an expert on
South American airports.

The newsroom writes **Buenos Aires** in pencil and immediately loses the eraser.

- @poland_event_queue: File Buenos Aires under "allegedly"

@world_tour
# prose-audit: Grade A — Two connected, non-repeating travel vignettes integrate each country's politics, Warsaw's response and the eventual exit without exposing the underlying dossier fields.
title: Ziobro's Extremely Unconfirmed World Tour
subtitle: Each new photograph is worse than the last. Each television map is much more confident.
face-image: img/poland/events/zbigniew-ziobro-2015.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 12
order: 71
max-visits: 2
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and ziobro_whereabouts_stage = 5 and ziobro_world_tour_updates < 2 and time >= ziobro_whereabouts_due_time
on-arrival: {!
Q.ziobro_previous_rumor_country = String(
    Q.ziobro_rumor_country || "the previous lead"
);
Q.ziobro_previous_rumor_departure = String(
    Q.ziobro_rumor_departure ||
    "The first lead dissolved before any authority confirmed an entry record."
);
const ziobroRumors = [
    ["El Salvador",
        "An official photograph from a San Salvador security conference contains one unexpected delegate. Ziobro is sitting in the front row beneath a badge issued to 'Z. Zero'. By afternoon a local think tank is advertising him as a European journalist with a lecture on sovereignty and foreign judges.",
        "Perhaps the attraction was visible from Warsaw: Nayib Bukele's immense popularity, a long state of exception and little patience for criticism from abroad. From inside El Salvador, the same arrangement has a drawback. A security state is exceptionally good at recording the foreigners who pass through it.",
        "Polish diplomats forward the invalidated document numbers and ask San Salvador to authenticate the badge. The presidential press office responds by posting an unrelated prison video. Three Polish channels put it beneath a BREAKING NEWS banner and call the matter substantially clarified.",
        "Immigration asks Z. Zero for biometrics, a valid passport and a less creative surname. The think tank deletes his biography, cancels the lecture and insists the front-row badge was always provisional. He leaves before the appointment at which the state of exception might finally have applied to him."],
    ["South Africa",
        "Cape Town airport CCTV catches Ziobro only as a reflection beneath the arrivals board. The image would prove nothing if an opposition researcher had not photographed the same coat in Parliament's public gallery the next morning. By lunch, reporters are asking who invited Poland's former justice minister to observe coalition government at work.",
        "South Africa's Government of National Unity has turned coalition management into a daily public quarrel. That may look like useful confusion from abroad. In practice it comes with an open press, parliamentary questions and enough rival parties to ensure that somebody is always delighted to leak a hotel invoice.",
        "Poland's embassy asks Pretoria to preserve the entry record. Before the foreign ministry can acknowledge receipt, an MP has already put the visit on the parliamentary order paper. Warsaw wanted quiet legal cooperation and instead receives a question broadcast live with supplementary questions.",
        "Reporters obtain the hotel bill, the public-gallery booking and three incompatible accounts of who arranged both. Then every party in the fragile unity cabinet discovers a rare common position: none wants to inherit Poland's former justice minister. Ziobro checks out while they are still congratulating one another on the breakthrough."],
    ["Thailand",
        "A Bangkok consultancy livestreams a seminar called 'Courts, Coalitions and Political Survival'. During the coffee break, the camera keeps running. It finds Ziobro at the whiteboard beneath five arrows that all lead from parliament back to parliament, explaining to an empty row of chairs that he is a European correspondent.",
        "Thailand's repeated coalition crises and court interventions can make political life look permanently improvised. The hotels are less relaxed. Guests are registered, passports are copied and immigration databases do not dissolve a booking merely because another prime minister has lost office.",
        "The Polish embassy passes on the invalidated passport details and requests confirmation without announcing an arrest from Warsaw. Bangkok acknowledges the note while Polish television is still debating whether the five arrows on the whiteboard reveal an escape route or merely a very bad diagram.",
        "Immigration matches the hotel registration to the cancelled document and asks Ziobro to explain his status. The consultancy deletes the stream, restores it after accusations of censorship, then deletes only the coffee break. He leaves on a late flight while its lawyers argue over which upload is now the official original."],
    ["Japan",
        "A Shinkansen reservation under 'Z. Z.' appears in a forwarded travel record. Station CCTV provides the less cryptic image of Ziobro boarding for Tokyo. The same initials are listed at an economic-security symposium beside a proposed lecture titled 'Sovereignty after Brussels' and a dietary request marked incomplete.",
        "Japan's conservative governing tradition may sound congenial to a former Polish right-wing minister. Its professional bureaucracy, close diplomatic relationship with Warsaw and devotion to correctly completed documents are less promising. The alleged traveller has chosen perfect order at the precise moment he requires useful ambiguity.",
        "The Polish embassy sends Tokyo the photograph and travel record. Tokyo replies with a numbered list of missing certifications; Warsaw supplies them. A Polish broadcaster calls the exchange a diplomatic standoff even though both governments are politely asking each other for attachment 2B.",
        "The symposium corrects its attendee list. Immigration schedules an interview with an exact time, platform number and diagram of the correct exit. Ziobro takes the exit marked airport. The train leaves precisely on schedule; for once in the journey, so does the man everyone is trying to locate."],
    ["Israel",
        "A cybersecurity conference in Herzliya publishes its closing photograph. Ziobro is standing beside a lawful-interception vendor beneath a badge identifying him as a Polish media correspondent. Delegates remember one question: whether a Pegasus licence includes support for locating witnesses who decline parliamentary invitations.",
        "Israel's battles over elected power and the Supreme Court give the sovereignty speech a familiar sound. Ziobro's old ministry also bought Pegasus, which provides notoriety in place of anonymity. Every technology reporter recognises him before the hotel receptionist has finished asking how to spell his name.",
        "Polish prosecutors use the formal mutual-assistance channel while the embassy checks the entry. Warsaw keeps the request narrowly legal. Polish television illustrates it with a winged horse, an orbiting satellite and the Justice Ministry, a sequence that explains Pegasus to nobody but fills eleven seconds perfectly.",
        "The conference withdraws the correspondent badge. Surveillance companies deny arranging the visit. Rival Israeli camps briefly agree that a fresh foreign Pegasus scandal would be inconvenient. The network Ziobro may have hoped to find becomes a queue of reporters asking who paid for his room, and he leaves before reaching the front."],
    ["South Korea",
        "A Polish student photographs Ziobro outside the Seoul courthouse hearing cases from the failed martial-law episode. The next picture shows him registering at the press desk as a TV Republika correspondent. A clerk remembers him explaining, unprompted, that resisting arrest can sometimes be a constitutional principle.",
        "South Korea has just watched parliament, courts and investigators confront a president over martial law. Conservative grievance and prosecutorial politics are plentiful; indulgence toward former officeholders is not. The court calendar alone is detailed enough to frighten anyone hoping to become an administrative oversight.",
        "The Polish embassy asks officials to preserve the registration and immigration data. Seoul returns a timestamped acknowledgment before Warsaw's first television panel reaches its advertising break. The speed is treated as suspicious only because the Polish side has grown accustomed to governments answering in geological time.",
        "Local coverage compares Ziobro's television appearances with the former president's resistance to arrest. Whatever sympathy the visit was meant to find disappears into a routine immigration appointment. He leaves Seoul after encountering the least convenient lesson available: political turmoil can produce more accountability rather than less."],
    ["Turkey",
        "A late-night livestream from an Istanbul hotel catches Ziobro at the edge of a legal forum, still wearing the interpretation headset. The programme calls him a visiting European journalist. The hotel invoice names a Polish political foundation which promptly announces that it has never heard of the hotel, the forum or the invoice.",
        "Recep Tayyip Erdoğan's long rule and transactional diplomacy can make Turkey look like a plausible refuge beyond the EU. Yet Ankara handles foreign fugitives as diplomatic files, not ideological houseguests. Agreement about judicial sovereignty is welcome; assuming it includes free accommodation is a category error.",
        "Warsaw avoids a televised ultimatum and sends the request through the applicable European extradition framework. Turkey confirms receipt without promising an outcome. Polish news tickers translate 'under consideration' into four mutually exclusive breaking-news banners and run all four before breakfast.",
        "Government media lose interest when the Polish charges replace the sovereignty speech. Opposition outlets ask who imported the dispute. Ankara sees no reason to spend diplomatic capital on an uninvited former minister, and Ziobro leaves before officials decide whether he is an extradition case, a bargaining chip or somebody else's reservation."]
].filter(function(rumor) {
    return rumor[0] != Q.ziobro_rumor_country;
});
const ziobroRumor =
    ziobroRumors[this.random.uint32() % ziobroRumors.length];
Q.ziobro_rumor_country = ziobroRumor[0];
Q.ziobro_rumor_discovery = ziobroRumor[1];
Q.ziobro_rumor_climate = ziobroRumor[2];
Q.ziobro_rumor_mfa = ziobroRumor[3];
Q.ziobro_rumor_departure = ziobroRumor[4];
const ziobroSecondRumor = Q.ziobro_world_tour_updates == 1;
Q.ziobro_final_escape_triggered =
    ziobroSecondRumor &&
    this.random.uint32() / 4294967296 < 0.20 ? 1 : 0;
Q.ziobro_final_escape_country = "";
Q.ziobro_final_escape_detail = "";
if (Q.ziobro_final_escape_triggered) {
    const finalDestinations = [
        ["Philippines",
            "The remaining evidence is a Manila boarding-pass stub and an email asking whether the television studio has an ocean view and no extradition desk in shot."],
        ["India",
            "The remaining evidence is an Indian e-visa receipt and a calendar invitation titled 'Comparative Judicial Reform — keynote, identity and venue to be confirmed'."]
    ];
    const finalDestination =
        finalDestinations[this.random.uint32() % finalDestinations.length];
    Q.ziobro_final_escape_country = finalDestination[0];
    Q.ziobro_final_escape_detail = finalDestination[1];
}
Q.ziobro_world_tour_updates += 1;
Q.ziobro_whereabouts_updates += 1;
Q.ziobro_whereabouts_last =
    Q.ziobro_final_escape_triggered
        ? Q.ziobro_final_escape_country + " — one last unconfirmed escape"
        : Q.ziobro_rumor_country + " — entirely unconfirmed";
if (Q.ziobro_world_tour_updates >= 2) {
    Q.ziobro_whereabouts_stage = 6;
    Q.ziobro_whereabouts_due_time = -1;
} else {
    Q.ziobro_whereabouts_due_time =
        (Number(Q.time) || 0) + 3 + this.random.uint32() % 4;
}
Q.news_headline = Q.ziobro_final_escape_triggered
    ? "The MFA reaches " + Q.ziobro_rumor_country +
        " one flight after Ziobro leaves for " +
        Q.ziobro_final_escape_country
    : "Ziobro is reportedly in " + Q.ziobro_rumor_country +
        "; the evidence declines to comment";
!}

= [+ date_label +] — A rumour with hand luggage

[? if ziobro_world_tour_updates = 1: The previous report was supposed to be the
last. Instead, today's rumour lands in **[+ ziobro_rumor_country +]** carrying
one blurry image, two confident commentators and no official confirmation.?]

[? if ziobro_world_tour_updates = 1: [+ ziobro_rumor_discovery +]?]

[? if ziobro_world_tour_updates = 1: [+ ziobro_rumor_climate +]?]

[? if ziobro_world_tour_updates = 1: [+ ziobro_rumor_mfa +]?]

[? if ziobro_world_tour_updates = 1: For now, the embassy says it is checking.
Television says it will have the answer after the break. Somewhere between
those statements lies the whole of the available evidence.?]

[? if ziobro_world_tour_updates = 2: Three to six months later, **[+
ziobro_previous_rumor_country +]** drops out of the story in the manner to which
this file has become accustomed. [+ ziobro_previous_rumor_departure +]?]

[? if ziobro_world_tour_updates = 2: Before Warsaw can close that folder, a new
report places Ziobro in **[+ ziobro_rumor_country +]**. Its principal advantage
over the previous report is that nobody has disproved it yet.?]

[? if ziobro_world_tour_updates = 2: [+ ziobro_rumor_discovery +]?]

[? if ziobro_world_tour_updates = 2: [+ ziobro_rumor_climate +]?]

[? if ziobro_world_tour_updates = 2: [+ ziobro_rumor_mfa +]?]

[? if ziobro_world_tour_updates = 2: The report survives just long enough to
acquire an ending of its own. [+ ziobro_rumor_departure +]?]

[? if ziobro_world_tour_updates = 2 and ziobro_final_escape_triggered = 0: The
file closes here, not because Ziobro has been found, but because an itinerary
made entirely from unconfirmed departures is no longer an itinerary. The next
anonymous airport photograph will have to find its own television programme.?]

[? if ziobro_world_tour_updates = 2 and ziobro_final_escape_triggered = 1:
The file is almost closed when one last airline alert arrives. The formal reply
from **[+ ziobro_rumor_country +]** has reached Warsaw one departure too late;
local authorities now believe Ziobro continued to **[+
ziobro_final_escape_country +]**.?]

[? if ziobro_world_tour_updates = 2 and ziobro_final_escape_triggered = 1: [+
ziobro_final_escape_detail +] A prosecutor opens one more diplomatic envelope.
The newsroom adds one last arrow, declines to number it and quietly retires the
word **final**.?]

- @poland_event_queue: File the rumour and confiscate the red string
